    "summary": "Totem pole carved of wood. At the head of the pole is an eagle, followed by a human intertwined with a killer whale. Below them is the face and front limbs of a wolf. The entire pole is decorated in blue, red and black paint, emphasising the mouths, eyes and ears of the figures in addition to the entire whale and the eagle&#039;s wings. The back of the pole is undecorated and has a shallow indentation.",
